ts and successful output generation provide independent crosschecks, not a presumption that an exit code proves circuit behavior.\n\n## Measurements and conclusions\n\n- Requirements read directly: inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md lines 6-16. Only ideal unloaded 1 V step acceptance at 1 ms (0.62..0.65 V) and every track width >=0.20 mm are declared.\n- inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb lines 667-706: five segments independently parsed from original S-expressions, all 0.25 mm. No excluded nets. Via is separately counted. audit.json /segments records all endpoints, nets and UUIDs. This is geometric compliance only.\n- Native pad inventory at PCB lines 210-225, 359-374, 587-613 matches exported schematic pins: IN J1.1/R1.1; OUT J1.2/R1.2/C1.1; GND J1.3/C1.2. Re-exported design.xml lines 164-175 and original work/netlist/design.xml /nets agree. R1=10k and C1=100n are also present in native schematic lines 955,1274 and native PCB values. No DNP parts.\n- IN travels on F.Cu to R1; OUT travels R1.2 to C1.1 with a T branch to J1.2. C1.2 travels 2.05 mm to GND via at (113,100), then saved B.Cu zone to J1.3. See PCB lines 699-809, zone UUID 38a83012-bcf9-4bb9-b9f4-50d49cd91d90; audit.json /zone. All 1558 samples of an explicitly defined route, with <=0.01 mm step, lie in saved fill. End point lies within J1.3 copper annulus (.7778 mm radius, .5 mm drill radius and .85 mm pad radius). Sampling supplements native DRC; it does not determine impedance or establish every possible geometric clearance.\n- Repeated KiCad DRC with schematic parity: zero violations, zero unconnected items, zero parity differences. See drc.json; original work/drc/drc.json agrees. Project drc_exclusions empty. Ignored check categories remain listed in native reports. All three visible footprints have courtyard rectangles; rendered placements/courtyards are separated and within the closed 20x12 mm outline. Front and back copper renders show the expected routing and J1.3 thermal connections. Native J1 drill/pad diameters are 1.0/1.7 mm, via .3/.6 mm; no specific fabrication process qualification is inferred.\n- Supplied transient deck is R1 IN OUT 10k, C1 OUT 0 100n, PWL 0..1 V over 1 ns, initial output zero, no load. Reading work/rc-step/result.raw independently gives 1025 samples through 5 ms, Vout(1ms)=0.632120134 V by interpolation, Vout(5ms)=0.993262120 V. Analytical instantaneous-step answer at 1 ms =0.632120559 V. Exact finite-ramp response at 1 ms =0.632120375 V; maximum absolute sample error versus exact finite-ramp solution is 0.763 microvolt. Thus the stimulus approximation is immaterial to the stated limit. See audit.json /waveform and review.py. Five-ms point has no declared acceptance bounds and is only informational.\n- Ideal instantaneous-step initial current =1 V/10 kohm=100 microampere, resistor peak dissipation=1''^2/10000=0.1 mW, stored capacitor energy=.5*100 nF*1''^2=50 nJ. These calculations do not assume copper thickness, component power rating or temperature rise, and establish no thermal or ampacity qualification.\n- No evidence-supported physical defect or additional concern identified under the captured scope. Candidate hashes before/after native audit are in audit.json, and final input hashes are in final-hashes.json.\n\n## Explicit coverage omissions\n\nNo zone refill (saved fill only); no manufactured hardware test; no thermal rise or ampacity validation; no copper thickness/stackup or fabricator-specific process, assembly, solder-joint, enclosure or mounting qualification; no exact purchased-part/package/rating verification beyond saved generic footprints. No impedance/parasitic extraction, return-path EMI qualification, ESD or source-transient testing. No tolerance, temperature, external load, ADC sampling or capacitor technology/bias modeling. ERC was read from supplied report, not independently rerun; ignored ERC/DRC categories were not globally enabled. No ngspice rerun was necessary: actual binary waveform was checked 